    "summary": "This community centers on MORSEL_TO_COOKIE, an externally defined callable that converts a Morsel object into a cookie. It depends on TIME.TIME for current-time calculations, TIME.STRPTIME and CALENDAR.TIMEGM for parsing and converting expiration dates, and MORSEL.KEY and MORSEL.VALUE for extracting cookie data. INT is a broadly reused Python built-in involved in type checks, validation, numeric conversion, redirect handling, proxy configuration, cookie expiration processing, and content-length comparisons. The available data describes technical relationships and implementation dependencies, but provides no evidence about legal compliance, organizational ownership, reputation, or malicious activity.",
