        },
        {
            "summary": "Cookie expiration supports both max-age and expires paths",
            "explanation": "MORSEL_TO_COOKIE uses TIME.TIME when a cookie's max-age value is truthy, obtaining the current time before adding the parsed integer lifetime. This indicates a relative-expiration path based on the current clock. [Data: Relationships (657); Entities (533, 584)]\n\nWhen max-age is absent and expires is truthy, MORSEL_TO_COOKIE calls TIME.STRPTIME with a visible GMT time template and then passes the parsed tuple to CALENDAR.TIMEGM. This provides an absolute-expiration path based on the cookie's expires value. The supplied data establishes these calls but does not provide evidence about malformed-date handling beyond the existence of tests for expected exception behavior. [Data: Relationships (658, 659); Entities (533, 585, 586)]"
        },
